    {
      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research obstacle representation and preprocessing. Starting from e7272600e1174704, evaluate contiguous row offsets plus sorted, deduplicated columns instead of per-row allocations. Preserve open-run traversal and explicit obstacle resets. Produce an interface that can enumerate obstacles within a column stripe or tile without rescanning entire rows. Separately measure faster standard-input parsing. Avoid quadratic obstacle storage where possible; retain correctness for arbitrary coordinate order, duplicates, blocked endpoints and n=1.\",\"B\":\"Research ARM64 NEON open-run scans from a53329fa10f644a9. Target integration into C's private stripe DP: accept an incoming left-boundary carry for the first open run, reset carry after every obstacle, and return the stripe's final carry. Keep scalar tails and short-run fallback. Reduce modulo after every scan addition so intermediates remain bounded. Measure scalar versus SIMD kernels independently; the current 25.71 ms SIMD candidate does not establish a gain over A's 24.49 ms scalar implementation.\",\"C\":\"Refine the two leading parallel designs independently. Use b0f0d71d84ea4ce4 as the pipeline reference and e73523535dc44046 as the tiled reference. Explore a small bounded set of batch sizes, tile sizes, thread counts and serial crossover thresholds on the fixed four-core target. Preserve release/acquire publication of boundary values, private DP ownership and correctness when OpenMP supplies fewer threads than requested. Measure sparse open-run traversal as a separate kernel substitution, not an assumed improvement.\",\"G\":\"Integrate through measured ablations: unchanged pipeline champion; pipeline plus A's obstacle representation; pipeline plus B's carry-aware SIMD kernel; then their combination. Compare against the unchanged tiled candidate as well. Include preprocessing, allocation and input costs in end-to-end measurements under the existing harness and budgets. Check stripe/tile boundaries, partial batches, short runs, duplicate obstacles, blocked endpoints and n=1 using existing permitted validation. Retain the fastest validated complete program; reject regressions and do not assume gains compose. Do not change compiler, target, tests, oracle or budgets.\",\"analysis\":\"The source solves Problem D, modular grid-path counting. Baseline time is 80.65 ms. The pipeline and tiled candidates achieve 13.547 and 13.567 ms, about 5.95× baseline; their approximately 0.15% separation is not persuasive without variability measurements. Sparse scalar traversal reaches 24.49 ms, versus 50.72 ms for the basic in-place dense variant. Open-run SIMD reaches 25.71 ms and masked SIMD 35.19 ms, so vectorization is not yet an established win. The strongest synthesis hypothesis is combining parallel scheduling with cheaper obstacle traversal, then testing SIMD separately. All variants must implement the full recurrence modulo 1000000007 for every valid input, rather than specialize to measured cases.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"b2f69c866533494da6cfa1068d12e9414dc93741b55e39c0d9a04c54aaa669a1\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research obstacle representation and preprocessing. Starting from e7272600e1174704, evaluate contiguous row offsets plus sorted, deduplicated columns instead of per-row allocations. Preserve open-run traversal and explicit obstacle resets. Produce an interface that can enumerate obstacles within a column stripe or tile without rescanning entire rows. Separately measure faster standard-input parsing. Avoid quadratic obstacle storage where possible; retain correctness for arbitrary coordinate order, duplicates, blocked endpoints and n=1.\",\"B\":\"Research ARM64 NEON open-run scans from a53329fa10f644a9. Target integration into C's private stripe DP: accept an incoming left-boundary carry for the first open run, reset carry after every obstacle, and return the stripe's final carry. Keep scalar tails and short-run fallback. Reduce modulo after every scan addition so intermediates remain bounded. Measure scalar versus SIMD kernels independently; the current 25.71 ms SIMD candidate does not establish a gain over A's 24.49 ms scalar implementation.\",\"C\":\"Refine the two leading parallel designs independently. Use b0f0d71d84ea4ce4 as the pipeline reference and e73523535dc44046 as the tiled reference. Explore a small bounded set of batch sizes, tile sizes, thread counts and serial crossover thresholds on the fixed four-core target. Preserve release/acquire publication of boundary values, private DP ownership and correctness when OpenMP supplies fewer threads than requested. Measure sparse open-run traversal as a separate kernel substitution, not an assumed improvement.\",\"G\":\"Integrate through measured ablations: unchanged pipeline champion; pipeline plus A's obstacle representation; pipeline plus B's carry-aware SIMD kernel; then their combination. Compare against the unchanged tiled candidate as well. Include preprocessing, allocation and input costs in end-to-end measurements under the existing harness and budgets. Check stripe/tile boundaries, partial batches, short runs, duplicate obstacles, blocked endpoints and n=1 using existing permitted validation. Retain the fastest validated complete program; reject regressions and do not assume gains compose. Do not change compiler, target, tests, oracle or budgets.\",\"analysis\":\"The source solves Problem D, modular grid-path counting. Baseline time is 80.65 ms. The pipeline and tiled candidates achieve 13.547 and 13.567 ms, about 5.95× baseline; their approximately 0.15% separation is not persuasive without variability measurements. Sparse scalar traversal reaches 24.49 ms, versus 50.72 ms for the basic in-place dense variant. Open-run SIMD reaches 25.71 ms and masked SIMD 35.19 ms, so vectorization is not yet an established win. The strongest synthesis hypothesis is combining parallel scheduling with cheaper obstacle traversal, then testing SIMD separately. All variants must implement the full recurrence modulo 1000000007 for every valid input, rather than specialize to measured cases.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"nonce\":\"2870c4067df14ca2bafb0a3e79fa3349\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"medium\",\"request_sha256\":\"b2f69c866533494da6cfa1068d12e9414dc93741b55e39c0d9a04c54aaa669a1\",\"session_id\":\"43aca875f83b450ba3cf30fc8907236c\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"663a6a47299d91acee19626e11b2e8bc2ba21d5a3744e88791ede70b9b297949\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":18511,\"output_tokens\":712,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":98}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"medium\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":19223,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
